  "body": "Found by the high-tier re-review of PR #973 (2026-11-12, its review comment); it is main's existing behaviour, not that PR's change.\n\n1. **A non-finite axis is not caught.** The NonFinite law (`crates/sim/src/verify/engine.rs` ~32-36) checks a move's `from` and `to` but not its tool `axis`. An axis like `[1e-12, 0, inf]` is read as tilted, and reach law (c) then convicts nothing - even for a shank that is convicted with an upright axis.\n2. **A non-unit axis is used as given.** Reach reads `a[2]` of the axis without normalising (`crates/sim/src/verify/reach.rs` ~139-142). A 7x-scaled axis with a 2e-9 rad tilt loses its `ShankHit` and keeps only a `SweepHit`.\n\nNeither is known to be reachable from a generator today (the generators are expected to emit unit, finite axes), which is why this is filed `P3`. If a generator, an importer or an MCP path can produce such an axis, a collision passes verify: re-rate `P1` and say so here.\n\nDone means: verify refuses a move whose axis is non-finite or of zero length by name (the NonFinite law covers `axis`), and either normalises a non-unit axis once at the door or refuses it; both pinned by tests (the two reproductions above convict); a search of the generators and the MCP/CL import paths recorded on the issue: can any of them emit a non-unit or non-finite axis.\n",
